  17: |
    apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
    kind: PrometheusRule
    metadata:
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/instance: RELEASE-NAME
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm
        app.kubernetes.io/name: paperless-ngx
        app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.0.0
        helm.sh/chart: paperless-ngx-0.0.0
      name: RELEASE-NAME-paperless-ngx
      namespace: NAMESPACE
    spec:
      groups:
        - name: paperless-ngx-workload
          rules:
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, deployment) (
                  kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace="NAMESPACE", deployment=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}
                  or
                  kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, deployment) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, deployment) (
                    kube_deployment_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_deployment:paperless_ngx_replicas_available:max
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, statefulset) (
                  kube_statefulset_status_replicas_ready{namespace="NAMESPACE", statefulset=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}
                  or
                  kube_statefulset_status_replicas_ready{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, statefulset) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, statefulset) (
                    kube_statefulset_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_statefulset:paperless_ngx_replicas_ready:max
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, persistentvolumeclaim) (
                  kubelet_volume_stats_used_bytes{namespace="NAMESPACE", persistentvolumeclaim=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}
                  / kubelet_volume_stats_capacity_bytes{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  or
                  kubelet_volume_stats_used_bytes{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  / kubelet_volume_stats_capacity_bytes{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, persistentvolumeclaim) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, persistentvolumeclaim) (
                    kube_persistentvolumeclaim_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_persistentvolumeclaim:paperless_ngx_volume_used:ratio
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, cronjob) (
                  kube_cronjob_status_last_successful_time{namespace="NAMESPACE", cronjob=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}
                  or
                  kube_cronjob_status_last_successful_time{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, cronjob) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, cronjob) (
                    kube_cronjob_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_cronjob:paperless_ngx_backup_last_success:max
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, job_name) (
                  kube_job_status_failed{namespace="NAMESPACE", job_name=~".*paperless-ngx-backup.*"}
                  or
                  kube_job_status_failed{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, job_name) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, job_name) (
                    kube_job_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx", label_app_kubernetes_io_component="backup"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_job_name:paperless_ngx_backup_failed:max
            - expr: |-
                max by (namespace, pod, container) (
                  increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace="NAMESPACE", pod=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}[1h])
                  or
                  increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace="NAMESPACE"}[1h])
                  * on (namespace, pod) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, pod) (
                    kube_pod_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                )
              record: namespace_pod_container:paperless_ngx_restarts:increase1h
        - name: paperless-ngx-alerts
          rules:
            - alert: PaperlessNgxDown
              annotations:
                description: 'The web UI, the REST API and the document consumer are all in this one pod, so nothing is being served and nothing is being ingested. Start with `kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} describe deployment {{ $labels.deployment }}` and the pod''s own events. The failures that stop a start rather than crash it are a database or broker that cannot be reached, a volume that cannot be attached — a ReadWriteOnce claim still held by the outgoing pod is the usual one — and a rejected secret. A deliberately stopped release (`replicaCount: 0`) fires this too; silence it there.'
                summary: paperless-ngx {{ $labels.deployment }} has no available replica
              expr: namespace_deployment:paperless_ngx_replicas_available:max{namespace="NAMESPACE"} == 0
              for: 5m
              labels:
                severity: critical
            - alert: PaperlessNgxAbsent
              annotations:
                description: 'Either the release was uninstalled, or kube-state-metrics is not running and every other alert in this group is disarmed along with this one. Check `kubectl get deployment -l app.kubernetes.io/name=paperless-ngx -A` first; if the Deployment is there, the gap is in the monitoring stack rather than in the archive. A release renamed with `nameOverride` on a cluster whose kube-state-metrics does not export object labels looks identical from here. This alert deliberately names no namespace: `absent()` synthesises its series from equality matchers alone, so with rule scoping turned off there is no namespace label to name.'
                summary: No paperless-ngx Deployment is being reported
              expr: absent(namespace_deployment:paperless_ngx_replicas_available:max{namespace="NAMESPACE"})
              for: 15m
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxCrashLooping
              annotations:
                description: '`kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} logs {{ $labels.pod }} -c {{ $labels.container }} --previous` shows why the last attempt died. For the application container the common causes are a database migration that cannot complete, a broker that refuses the password, and a data volume whose ownership does not match `runAsUser` — the last of which appears as a permission error on `/usr/src/paperless/data` rather than as anything about Kubernetes.'
                summary: '{{ $labels.container }} in {{ $labels.pod }} is crash-looping'
              expr: |-
                max by (namespace, pod, container) (
                  kube_pod_container_status_waiting_reason{namespace="NAMESPACE", pod=~".*paperless-ngx.*", reason="CrashLoopBackOff"}
                  or
                  kube_pod_container_status_waiting_reason{namespace="NAMESPACE", reason="CrashLoopBackOff"}
                  * on (namespace, pod) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, pod) (
                    kube_pod_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                ) > 0
              for: 15m
              labels:
                severity: critical
            - alert: PaperlessNgxRestarting
              annotations:
                description: 'More than three restarts in an hour, without the sustained backoff that would fire PaperlessNgxCrashLooping. Check `kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} describe pod {{ $labels.pod }}` for the last terminated state. If it is `OOMKilled`, the memory limit is below what a document in the consumption directory costs to process: raise `resources.limits.memory`, or lower `paperless.tasks.workers`, which multiplies it.'
                summary: '{{ $labels.container }} in {{ $labels.pod }} restarted repeatedly in the last hour'
              expr: namespace_pod_container:paperless_ngx_restarts:increase1h{namespace="NAMESPACE"} > 3
              for: 10m
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxOOMKilled
              annotations:
                description: OCR holds a whole rasterised document in memory, so the peak is set by the largest document anyone feeds it and by `paperless.tasks.workers`, which multiplies that peak. A kill during consumption leaves the document in the consumption directory and it is retried on the next scan — which reproduces the kill. Raise `resources.limits.memory` in namespace {{ $labels.namespace }}, or move the offending file out of the way first.
                summary: '{{ $labels.container }} in {{ $labels.pod }} was killed for exceeding its memory limit'
              expr: |-
                max by (namespace, pod, container) (
                  kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason{namespace="NAMESPACE", pod=~".*paperless-ngx.*", reason="OOMKilled"}
                  or
                  kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason{namespace="NAMESPACE", reason="OOMKilled"}
                  * on (namespace, pod) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, pod) (
                    kube_pod_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                ) > 0
              for: 5m
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxVolumeFillingUp
              annotations:
                description: '`kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} edit pvc {{ $labels.persistentvolumeclaim }}` and raise `spec.resources.requests.storage` if the StorageClass allows expansion. Which volume this is decides what happens when it fills: the media claim stops documents being archived, the data claim stops the search index being written, and the consume claim stops new files being accepted.'
                summary: '{{ $labels.persistentvolumeclaim }} is over 85% full'
              expr: namespace_persistentvolumeclaim:paperless_ngx_volume_used:ratio{namespace="NAMESPACE"} > 0.85
              for: 15m
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxVolumeAlmostFull
              annotations:
                description: At this point consumption fails and, on the data volume, the search index can be left half-written — which is repaired with `document_index reindex` after there is room again. Expand `kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} get pvc {{ $labels.persistentvolumeclaim }}` now.
                summary: '{{ $labels.persistentvolumeclaim }} is over 95% full'
              expr: namespace_persistentvolumeclaim:paperless_ngx_volume_used:ratio{namespace="NAMESPACE"} > 0.95
              for: 5m
              labels:
                severity: critical
            - alert: PaperlessNgxBackupFailed
              annotations:
                description: '`kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} logs job/{{ $labels.job_name }}` has the reason. The ones that recur rather than resolve themselves: the export volume is full, which shows as an OSError partway through and is the same fix as PaperlessNgxVolumeFillingUp; the pod could not be scheduled, which under the default `backup.coScheduleWithApp` means the application pod was not running at the scheduled hour; the run outlived `backup.activeDeadlineSeconds`, which a first full export of a large archive genuinely can. In `zip` mode also check the scratch volume — the whole export is assembled there before it is compressed, and an evicted pod rather than a failed one is what running out of it looks like.'
                summary: paperless-ngx backup {{ $labels.job_name }} failed
              expr: namespace_job_name:paperless_ngx_backup_failed:max{namespace="NAMESPACE"} > 0
              for: 5m
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxBackupStale
              annotations:
                description: '`kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} get cronjob {{ $labels.cronjob }}` and check SUSPEND, LAST SCHEDULE and ACTIVE together. Suspended is the common one. An ACTIVE run that never finishes blocks every later run under `concurrencyPolicy: Forbid`, and the Job it is waiting on is usually Pending because the application pod moved to another node — the export mounts the same ReadWriteOnce claims and cannot follow it. Nothing here means documents are being lost; it means the last copy of them is getting older.'
                summary: paperless-ngx backup {{ $labels.cronjob }} has not succeeded in over two days
              expr: (time() - namespace_cronjob:paperless_ngx_backup_last_success:max{namespace="NAMESPACE"}) > 172800
              for: 1h
              labels:
                severity: critical
            - alert: PaperlessNgxBackupSuspended
              annotations:
                description: The schedule is paused, so no export is being taken. Six hours of tolerance is there so a maintenance window does not page anybody; past that it is a suspension somebody forgot to lift. Clear `backup.suspend` and upgrade, or `kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} patch cronjob {{ $labels.cronjob }} -p '{"spec":{"suspend":false}}'` if the release itself is mid-change.
                summary: paperless-ngx backup {{ $labels.cronjob }} is suspended
              expr: |-
                max by (namespace, cronjob) (
                  kube_cronjob_spec_suspend{namespace="NAMESPACE", cronjob=~".*paperless-ngx.*"}
                  or
                  kube_cronjob_spec_suspend{namespace="NAMESPACE"}
                  * on (namespace, cronjob) group_left ()
                  max by (namespace, cronjob) (
                    kube_cronjob_labels{namespace="NAMESPACE", label_app_kubernetes_io_name="paperless-ngx"}
                  )
                ) > 0
              for: 6h
              labels:
                severity: warning
            - alert: PaperlessNgxDatastoreDown
              annotations:
                description: '`kubectl -n {{ $labels.namespace }} describe statefulset {{ $labels.statefulset }}`. A bundled Valkey being down stops every document from being processed while the web UI keeps working, which is the confusing half of this. A bundled PostgreSQL being down stops everything. Both are single-replica evaluation-tier workloads: if this is a production archive, that is the finding, not the outage.'
                summary: paperless-ngx datastore {{ $labels.statefulset }} has no ready replica
              expr: namespace_statefulset:paperless_ngx_replicas_ready:max{namespace="NAMESPACE"} == 0
              for: 5m
              labels:
                severity: critical
